013</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B13"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Snounou</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Beck</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The use of PCR genotyping in the assessment of recrudescence or reinfection after antimalarial drug treatment</article-title><source>Parasitol Today</source><year>1998</year><volume>14</volume><fpage>462</fpage><lpage>467</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17040849</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0169-4758(98)01340-4</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Abdu-Aguye</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name><name><surname>Gebi</surname><given-names>UI</given-names></name><name><surname>Wuyat</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Agbo</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><source>An open-label uncontrolled trial confirming efficacy and safety of the 4-dose regimen of Coartem&#x000ae; in the treatment of acute Plasmodium falciparum malaria in patients aged &#x0003e; 2 years in Zaria Nigeria</source><year>2000</year><publisher-name>Report of a Clinical Trial, Novartis Pharma AG Nigeria study Report</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B15"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Eke</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Akhidue</surname><given-names>V</given-names></name><name><surname>Ukiwo</surname><given-names>UE</given-names></name><name><surname>Akosubo</surname><given-names>IJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Izuora</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Akpan</surname><given-names>PU</given-names></name><name><surname>Ufford</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Ugwumba</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Dennis</